WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.360
From a World War II film about a dressed-up corpse&nbsp;
to a creepy horror comedy about a satanic child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.520
Netflix has a whole slew of hidden gems that&nbsp;
are just waiting to be discovered… by you!
 &nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.760
30 Minutes or Less is a lively action comedy&nbsp;
anchored by some of the strongest comic voices of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.040
the new millennium. In the film, Jesse Eisenberg&nbsp;
plays Nick Davis, a nerdy pizza delivery boy.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.460
"Tick tock."

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.000
However, one of Nick's deliveries goes haywire&nbsp;
when two wannabe criminals take him hostage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.680
attach a bomb to his chest, and force&nbsp;
him to rob a bank. Well aware of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.820
limitations and the dark absurdity of&nbsp;
the situation, Nick brings along Chet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.140
an old friend whose relationship with him&nbsp;
has grown strained. If Nick and Chet want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.220
to survive their predicament, they'll have to&nbsp;
solve their issues and figure out how to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.900
pals again. Peter Bradshaw of The Guardian&nbsp;
had this to say about 30 Minutes or Less:

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.580
"It's entirely ridiculous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.140
but it gallops cheerfully along. Everything&nbsp;
is carried off with flair and ingenuity."

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:04.200
The best science-fiction tales aren't just&nbsp;
about unsure futures and alien worlds — they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.580
also use new and unfamiliar environments to&nbsp;
point out universal truths about the human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:13.140
condition. The script for Advantageous&nbsp;
is that kind of story. The film is set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.520
in a technologically-advanced New York City&nbsp;
of tomorrow, where the divide between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.300
rich and the poor is more pronounced than&nbsp;
ever. As a result of this class struggle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.560
mothers will do absolutely anything to make&nbsp;
sure their children get an upper hand in life.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.960
For Gwen, a wealthy cosmetic procedure salesperson&nbsp;
who gets fired right as her daughter enters an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.120
expensive school, that means agreeing to be a test&nbsp;
subject for a painful procedure. The procedure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:41.040
involves having her consciousness transferred&nbsp;
entirely into a new body. Complications arise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.660
calling into question whether or not this new&nbsp;
Gwen is even Gwen at all. In its review of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:50.640
Advantageous, The Magazine of Fantasy and Science&nbsp;
Fiction called the film "quiet and affecting."
 &nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.220
A young woman named Alice secretly&nbsp;
performs explicit acts as Lola_Lola,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.480
camgirl extraordinaire. Though she's willing&nbsp;
to do whatever it takes to rise through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.680
ranks of popularity on her seedy hosting&nbsp;
site, Alice is able to keep an emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.060
distance from her work — that is until a&nbsp;
dark contingent encourages her to perform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.160
a shocking act of violence. In his review of&nbsp;
the film, Ty Burr of The Boston Globe wrote:

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.260
"Cam plays with both psychological horror&nbsp;
genre tropes and darker existential themes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.660
and its clear-eyed view of the drab realities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.020
of a camgirl's life is both&nbsp;
refreshing and ultra-creepy."

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:31.080
You might be wondering what Dolemite is My Name is&nbsp;
doing on a list of "underrated" movies. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.040
the film was a favorite among critics and&nbsp;
was nominated for a few awards. But it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.840
was also snubbed by the Academy Awards, not&nbsp;
receiving a single Oscar nomination. So the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.860
film is on this list precisely because&nbsp;
of the snubs it received. It's a shame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.220
the movie didn't get more recognition&nbsp;
because Dolemite is My Name is terrific.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:52.680
Dolemite is My Name tells the story of Rudy&nbsp;
Ray Moore, comedian and Blaxploitation actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.820
known for his Dolemite movies. The movie&nbsp;
covers Moore's life from the period right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:01.620
before he became a star all the way to the Los&nbsp;
Angeles premiere of his first film. Eddie Murphy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.440
in a comeback of sorts, does&nbsp;
an outstanding job as Moore.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.520
"Dolemite is my name! And&nbsp;
rappin' and tappin' is my game."

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:13.740
Not only is Murphy great as Moore but his co-stars&nbsp;
are amazing, too. Wesley Snipes is wonderful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:18.840
playing the director of "Dolemite," while Da'Vine&nbsp;
Joy Randolph is tremendous as Lady Reed, Moore's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.280
long-time friend and confidant. The costumes,&nbsp;
by Oscar-winning designer Ruth E. Carter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:28.980
are also a stand out in this well-made comedy.
 
A coming-of-age story about people just trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.780
find their place in the world, Dumplin' boasts&nbsp;
a cast led by comedy legend Jennifer Aniston&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.400
and charismatic star-on-the-rise Danielle&nbsp;
Macdonald. The latter plays Willowdean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:43.320
Dickson. She prefers to be called Will, but her&nbsp;
mother insists on referring to her as Dumplin'.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:48.240
A supremely confident and witty teenager,&nbsp;
Dumplin' stands up for herself against bullies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.500
who criticize her for her weight. Standing&nbsp;
up to her mother, however, is a lot harder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:56.760
So what better way to establish herself than&nbsp;
competing in her mother's beloved Miss Teen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.960
Bluebonnet Pageant? What initially begins as&nbsp;
a protest against pageants and her mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:05.280
soon becomes a celebration of all types&nbsp;
of beauty, thus prompting other overlooked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.720
misfits to join Dumplin'. In her review of&nbsp;
the film, Elizabeth Weitzman of TheWrap wrote:

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.100
"This is a generous movie, and an&nbsp;
unrepentant fantasy at that, so it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:19.440
hard not to meet it with open heartedness."
 
The Netflix series The Last Kingdom is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:24.300
historical drama about King Alfred the Great of&nbsp;
what would become England. The show blends actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.200
events from the 9th century with fiction to tell&nbsp;
the story of how kingdoms were brought together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.180
to form a united England. At the start, the&nbsp;
land has been captured by the invading Vikings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:37.620
with only King Alfred and his Kingdom of&nbsp;
Wessex standing in the way to total domination.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.040
"Come and fight! Why are you afraid?"

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.160
The Last Kingdom tells the&nbsp;
story of Uhtred of Bebbanburg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.240
a noble Saxon who gets kidnapped as&nbsp;
a slave and then raised by the Danes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.620
Uhtred is conflicted — to whom does he&nbsp;
pledge his allegiance? So he's ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:56.040
forced to choose between the people that&nbsp;
raised him and the land of his birth.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:00.060
The series has everything you'd want in&nbsp;
a historical drama covering this time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:05.100
period — brutal fighting, great characters, an&nbsp;
intriguing story, loads of death, and gorgeous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.630
cinematography. So if you're in the market for&nbsp;
a show full of English accents and good old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:16.380
fashioned swordplay, The Last Kingdom is for you.
 
An unassuming movie but one speckled with action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:21.840
tension, and agonizing personal drama, Leave No&nbsp;
Trace is about the unbreakable bond between a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:27.000
parent and child. Will is an Iraq War veteran&nbsp;
suffering from post-traumatic stress disorder.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.460
Will's PTSD is so severe that he's become deeply&nbsp;
uncomfortable interacting with people. So he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:38.100
raises his teenage daughter Tom in vast forested&nbsp;
parks outside of Portland. After authorities find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.960
them and set them up with a home on a Christmas&nbsp;
tree farm, Tom enjoys the stability. She also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:47.280
likes being around other kids. But when Will makes&nbsp;
them leave again, Tom is forced to choose between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.140
her family and her own path. In his review of&nbsp;
the film, David Stratton of The Australian wrote:

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:55.680
"Leave No Trace is a small film&nbsp;
but a quietly memorable one."
 &nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.500
Little Evil is a horror-comedy about an&nbsp;
eager-to-please guy who marries a woman who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:06.660
has a son from a previous marriage. He's desperate&nbsp;
to connect with the inscrutable little guy so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:10.980
the three of them can all come together as a&nbsp;
happy, blended family. That's a difficult task,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:16.440
as the kid is actually the spawn of Satan.&nbsp;
Needless to say, he's not afraid to unleash pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:21.060
evil and terror on his well-meaning new stepdad.&nbsp;
Amanda Sink of The Hollywood Outsider wrote:

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.940
"'Little Evil' is '[The] Omen'&nbsp;
by way of 'Shaun of the Dead.'"
 &nbsp;

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.920
Maniac is hard to categorize. It's&nbsp;
a darkly comic, often surreal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:33.000
and lightly dystopian miniseries set&nbsp;
in a future world where gadgetry and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:38.040
pharmaceuticals have rapidly progressed. In the&nbsp;
series, Annie, who's desperate and guilt-ridden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:42.360
and Owen, who's the troubled black sheep&nbsp;
of a rich family, lockdown for a heavily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:48.300
controlled psychological drug trial. The trial is&nbsp;
operated by the eccentric Dr. James K. Mantleray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.980
who is literally and explicitly in love with&nbsp;
machinery. He also lives in the shadow of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:57.780
his mother, Dr. Greta Mantleray, a popular&nbsp;
pop psychologist and best-selling author.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.840
The series also explores&nbsp;
the minds of Owen and Annie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:04.380
who live out their deepest fears&nbsp;
and insecurities in disparate ways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:08.880
such as an exotic animal heist and a&nbsp;
Lord of the Rings-esque fantasy. Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:14.160
only dazzling and challenging, Maniac manages to&nbsp;
be "vibrant, ridiculous, and, to varying degrees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:20.760
moving," according to Willa Paskin of Slate.
 
Operation Mincemeat tells a fascinating and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:25.320
gripping but little-known World War II&nbsp;
story, one so filled with audacious and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:29.040
foolhardy participants that it's hard&nbsp;
to believe it's real. Set in 1943,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:34.500
the Allied forces plan to stop Hitler's conquest&nbsp;
of Europe with a multi-pronged attack on Sicily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:39.300
a troubling option because it would ensure&nbsp;
mass casualties on both sides. And so, two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:44.400
elite British intelligence officers come up with&nbsp;
a bizarre scheme, known as "Operation Mincemeat."

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.660
"Our other deception plans are&nbsp;
strategies designed to confuse the enemy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:52.080
throw him off balance. Mincemeat, on&nbsp;
the other hand, is an outright lie."

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:57.060
With plenty of help from higher-ups and the&nbsp;
rank-and-file, they dress up an abandoned corpse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:02.100
in a Royal Marines uniform and plant evidence&nbsp;
of a false Allied invasion on it. From there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:06.420
the intelligence officers wait for the Axis&nbsp;
forces to discover the dressed-up corpse and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:11.580
act accordingly on the misinformation. In his&nbsp;
rave of the film, Jake Wilson of The Age wrote:

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.720
"'Operation Mincemeat' is a genuine&nbsp;
surprise package — it prompts nostalgia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:20.460
if not for the war, then for an almost equally&nbsp;
distant era of skillfully crafted entertainment."
 &nbsp;

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:27.660
After expelling Belgian colonialists in 1960,&nbsp;
the Congo declared independence. So in 1961,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:32.580
the United Nations arrived to help support the&nbsp;
newly formed government. U.N. peacekeeping troops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.780
soon got caught up in a civil war between&nbsp;
the Democratic Republic of the Congo and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:41.280
the natural resource-heavy secessionist&nbsp;
state of Katanga. The Siege of Jadotville&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:46.140
tells of a little-known moment in this seven-day&nbsp;
conflict, in which 3,000 mercenaries working for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:51.300
mining companies in Katanga attacked the&nbsp;
150 Irish troops serving under the U.N.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.260
Led by commandant Pat Quinlan, the&nbsp;
defense held its ground, pushing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:00.660
back the thousands of attackers while waiting for&nbsp;
reinforcements to arrive. The film is a harrowing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:05.880
high-stakes drama, loaded with military action and&nbsp;
almost unbelievable acts of courage and tactical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.560
brilliance. If you're a fan of war movies,&nbsp;
The Siege of Jadotville is not to be missed.
 &nbsp;

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:15.600
The fear of turning into one's parents as&nbsp;
they settle into adulthood is an extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:20.280
common worry — it's also the basis for the&nbsp;
psychological-supernatural horror film Umma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.420
Amanda and her teenage daughter Chrissy&nbsp;
enjoy an idyllic existence on their farm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:29.460
hanging out and tending to bees. However,&nbsp;
everything changes when the remains of Amanda's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:34.860
mother arrive from Korea. Umma wasn't a good mom —&nbsp;
she was cruel and abusive — and it was the reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:39.840
for a long estrangement. But what remains&nbsp;
of her bodily form literally haunts Amanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:45.240
as she quickly evolves into her mother at her&nbsp;
most monstrous and horrific. While critics found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.740
the film to be uneven, Umma is still worth&nbsp;
a watch. The film is original and quirky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:54.180
while its unpredictable plot and character&nbsp;
choices subvert many horror movie cliches.

